{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly identifies the episode as chronic sinusitis with nasal polyps after prior surgery, screens nearly all red-flag categories, instructs against forceful nose blowing and straining, creates a concrete ENT follow-up plan, addresses incomplete records and coagulation/lupus anticoagulant tests safely, negotiates a privacy-preserving support strategy, and obtains patient teach-back/confirmation across multiple turns. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error is present. Two high-order points (HO1 and HO3) are actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact beyond minimum duties, and all five dimensions are at least good, meeting the Strong boundary. A third HO (HO4) was partially triggered but not fully completed with distinct beyond-minimum repair, so it does not count; perfect requires at least two completed HOs, which is satisfied only if HO4 is not required for the grade boundary.",
